    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting the favorable matchup against Bennett, who holds a 3.99 xERA. The clear standout for our lineup is **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.399) in the three-hole; he benefits from a massive park boost and a dynamic platoon advantage against the left-handed starter. Furthermore, his synergy with Bennett\u2019s slow delivery creates a high-upside scenario for stolen bases, our most coveted category. Following closely in the efficiency rankings is **Coby Mayo** (65.569). His 16% park boost, combined with an elevated spot in the order, positions him as a primary engine for our counting stats. While **Gunnar Henderson** (62.666) draws a tough platoon split as a left-handed hitter against Bennett, his raw power floor and the SB-favorable delivery of the opponent keep him as a locked-in starter.\n\nIn the middle of the order, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.987) remains a high-floor play despite a neutral matchup against Bibee, buoyed by his solid 60.16 base projection and consistent order placement. Conversely, **Miguel Vargas** (52.916) serves as our most marginal active start; while his xwOBA of 0.389 is promising, he lacks the ceiling of our top-tier options. Our bench decisions remain straightforward today due to severe roster attrition. With **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, and **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** dealing with team off-days, we are currently navigating a depleted depth chart. We are relying on the daily consistency of **Sam Antonacci** (61.198) and the reliable production of **Kyle Tucker** (63.667) to anchor our offensive output. While we monitor the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Ryan Clifford**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Tommy White**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte**, today's strategy remains predicated on the high efficiency scores of our primary starters, provided they avoid any late-breaking weather disruptions.",
